    {"input": ["[\"push\",\"pop\",\"size\",\"push\",\"push\",\"set\",\"get\",\"get\"]", "[[5],[],[],[6],[7],[0,60],[0],[1]]"], "output": "[null,5,0,null,null,null,60,7]"}
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Keep three fields: a pointer to the elements, the number of elements in use, and the capacity.",
    "When size == capacity, grow the capacity by a factor (doubling is classic) with realloc.",
    "Assign realloc's result to a temporary first: if it returns NULL, your old block is still valid.",
    "vecFree must free the element array and the struct itself."
  ],
  "constraints": ["Up to 20 000 pushes per test", "get/set/pop are only called with valid indices / on a non-empty vector", "pushRange [lo, hi] is a harness shortcut that pushes lo, lo+1, ..., hi-1"],
  "memory": "Growing must be **amortized O(1)**: the number of reallocations must grow only logarithmically with the number of pushes. `vecFree` must release everything."
}
@@ description
Implement a growable array of `int`s, the C version of C++'s `std::vector` or Python's `list`.

```c
typedef struct IntVec IntVec;      // you define struct IntVec

IntVec *vecCreate(void);
void vecPush(IntVec *v, int value);          // append at the end
int  vecGet(const IntVec *v, int index);
void vecSet(IntVec *v, int index, int value);
int  vecPop(IntVec *v);                      // remove and return the last element
int  vecSize(const IntVec *v);
void vecFree(IntVec *v);
```

The test harness only sees an **opaque** `IntVec *`: it never looks inside your struct. This is how C libraries hide their internals (`FILE *` works the same way).

**The catch:** calling `realloc` on every push copies the whole array each time, making n pushes cost O(n²). The harness counts your allocations: grow the capacity *geometrically* so the number of reallocations stays tiny.
@@ prelude
typedef struct IntVec IntVec;
IntVec *vecCreate(void);
void vecPush(IntVec *v, int value);
int  vecGet(const IntVec *v, int index);
void vecSet(IntVec *v, int index, int value);
int  vecPop(IntVec *v);
int  vecSize(const IntVec *v);
void vecFree(IntVec *v);
